-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Incredible Shrinking Fireman
  Publisher   Mastertronic
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Incredible Shrinking Fireman, The (1986)(Mastertronic).z80
  MD5         fc8e7535fc42afb60c12625b5fdfd064

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same file;
              probe 0xB950, Kempston bot keyed to updates; no state addresses,
              so lockstep not checked)

  Changes     1.1: works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next 26.11)
              1.2: the hooks hand back the CPU speed the game was running at,
              instead of always dropping to 3.5 MHz

  Note        Works on NextZXOS v2.10 from 1.1. Plays at the original's pace:
              +0.0%, +0.3% and +0.4% over 600 game updates (quiet thirds up to
              +1.2%, busy thirds up to +0.2%), in JNext, 2026-11-07. Known
              issues: none found in testing; over 20-update stretches the
              build was at most about 6% behind the original. Missing: no
              Enhanced colour set; the pace runs could not be checked for
              lockstep (no state addresses); earlier builds ran on a real Next
              for Dean, and the faults he found were fixed, but this build has
              not; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  No enemies

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

